WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.329
Those are the words of Klaus Schwab,

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.129
head of the World Economic Forum in

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.169
COVID 19 the Great Reset.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.179
People assume

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.309
we are just going back

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.260
to the good old world which we had,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.829
and everything will be normal again

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.689
in how we are used

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.619
to normal.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.519
And the old fashioned system

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.149
is, let's say, fiction.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.529
It will not happen.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.149
At the latest World Economic Forum

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.039
meeting in Davos, Schwab set the

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.479
tone for the conference with his

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.549
glowing introduction of the opening

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.269
speaker.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.429
We now welcome

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.319
His Excellency Xi

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.269
Jinping, president of

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.579
the People's Republic of China.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.899
Xi laid out his vision of a

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.789
coordinated global economy.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.619
Major economies should

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.839
see the world as one community

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.789
and coordinate the objectives,

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.069
intensity and pace

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.199
of fiscal and monetary policies.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.209
This ideal of a united globe

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.279
with a coordinated economy managed

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.319
by experts captures Schwab's

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.209
vision of the post-COVID world.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.159
We have to redefine

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.689
our social contract.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.849
These grand proclamations,

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.889
the ominous book title and Schwab's

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.689
odd personal style have led many

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.279
people to speculate that the Great

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.519
Reset is part of a conspiracy

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.199
of global financial elites and

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.029
politicians to depopulate

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.609
the planet so they can more easily

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.249
institute one world government

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.319
or even that COVID was engineered

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.309
to that end.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.139
Remember the stated goal by these

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.188
people

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:39.449
Billionaire transhumanist elites,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.979
the globalists that all get together

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:41.729
every year.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.499
As the population of the planet,.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.079
A transhumanist revolution

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.669
to make people chronically sick that

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.739
results in the death of the vast

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.809
majority of the world population and

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.819
out of that cataclysm,

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.260
a new super race.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:57.899
I don't buy it.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.699
Imagine the amount of coordination

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.229
and airtight secrecy needed for

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.399
these kinds of far reaching

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.229
conspiracies of global domination

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.609
to succeed.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.229
They'd be exposed and fall apart,

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.399
especially in the age of the

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.349
internet, instead of spinning

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.939
our wheels searching for a secret

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:12.899
agenda.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.979
Let's just look at the one that's

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:14.999
right out in the open.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.219
I think we are moving from

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.259
short term to long term,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.260
from

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.099
shareholder capitalism to

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.449
stakeholder capitalism.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.399
What China, the World Economic

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.199
Forum and Massachusetts Senator

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.999
Elizabeth Warren have in common is

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.199
that they favor so-called

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.119
stakeholder capitalism,

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.769
which is the euphemism for making

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.509
companies answer first to special

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.319
interests.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.909
They want to reorganize corporate

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.649
boards to include representatives

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.509
from labor, environmental and social

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.979
justice groups.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.839
Warren proposed a bill to require

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.639
40 percent of large corporate board

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.249
seats be elected by workers.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.439
In  China, the state simply owns

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.329
or controls a majority stake in

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.339
most of the country's largest firms.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.529
The World Economic Forum and many

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.149
state leaders believe global

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.339
coordination and global governance

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.259
is essential to manage global

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.059
problems, climate change,

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.369
international financial instability

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.259
and future pandemics.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.119
A crucial flaw in Schwab's

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.979
Great Reset is that it puts

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.689
too much faith in the ability of

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.609
governments to re-engineer society

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.199
in a way that better serves the

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.179
needs and desires of all citizens.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.099
He wants a rethinking of capitalism

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.989
that escapes the tyranny of GDP

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.939
growth so that companies create

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.649
goods and services for the common

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.569
good instead of maximizing

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.829
profits.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.659
The phrase "common good"

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:34.889
points to his fundamental

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.539
misunderstanding of capitalism,

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.649
which is nothing new.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.209
Central planners were using this

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.039
idea to maximize their own power

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.546
at the expense of individual freedom

00:03:42.547 --> 00:03:44.459
back in the 1940s, when

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.289
Nobel Prize winning economist F.A.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.299
Hayek wrote "The Road to Serfdom,"

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.009
which would go on to sell over two

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.010
million copies.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.679
Every single one of the billions of

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.479
people who populate this planet have

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.189
unique goals and desires that are

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.319
impossible to reduce to a unified

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.209
whole. Whether that's GDP or

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.099
whatever supposedly holistic metrics

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.989
the WEF wants to replace it with,

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.278
profits are a signal to

00:04:17.279 --> 00:04:18.778
entrepreneurs that they are

00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:20.699
satisfying the disparate needs

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:21.700
of their customers.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.889
Schwab is right that the war is the

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:38.789
health of the state.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.169
As the writer Randolph Bourne once

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.549
put it, and the government's

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.559
response to COVID has been similar

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.449
to military conflict in terms of

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.249
the cost and the chaos it's

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.169
engendered. World Wars one and

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:50.939
two and the Great Depression ushered

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.979
in a powerful modern welfare

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.349
and warfare state that irreversibly

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.359
altered America and the world.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.339
But I'm more optimistic this

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.339
time.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:01.719
Thanks in large part to the power of

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.639
technology to provide everyday

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.859
citizens with an exit instead

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.419
of the Great Reset, in which

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.819
sclerotic 20th century institutions

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.949
accumulate even more power.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.899
I think we're entering

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.699
the Great Escape.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:16.989
This is possible because

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.329
technological progress is outpacing

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.189
the ability of the state to control

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.389
and regulate it.

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:23.769
Governments will have no choice but

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.059
to abandon their efforts to

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.649
construct physical and metaphorical

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:27.699
walls.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.109
Technology can be designed to

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:31.479
facilitate decentralization

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.369
in which the flow of money and

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.829
information can't be controlled.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.839
Ideas emerge from the bottom up,

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.949
expecting governments and

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:40.839
international bodies to orient

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.699
every large company towards

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.649
some widely agreed upon common

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.539
good assumes that many of

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.639
the very institutions that bungled

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.469
that COVID 19 response can

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.299
competently handle the planet's

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.459
most intractable problems.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.439
My hope is that after witnessing

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.149
the colossal failure of governments

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.919
in the face of a global crisis, many

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.239
more people will be looking for a

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:02.349
different approach.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:03.639
There's evidence everywhere of the

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:04.569
great escape.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:06.489
The US population shift away from

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.229
expensive, restrictive and poorly

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:10.029
governed states and cities, spurred

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.859
on by the rise of remote work.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.299
The exodus from government run

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.889
schools, the growing use of

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:17.049
cryptocurrency, the popularity

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:18.789
of encrypted private communication

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.619
platforms and the expanding

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.449
reach of independent voices in

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.129
our increasingly decentralized

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.409
media. Hayek called central planning

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:28.449
the fatal conceit, writing

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:28.497
that.

00:06:28.498 --> 00:06:29.498
And

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.019
Schwab even touches on this idea,

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.020
writing that.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.359
He dubs this "quantum

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.519
politics," but never quite explains

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.499
how policymakers will realistically

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.299
overcome this dilemma.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.129
Maybe there's record low trust

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.779
in our institutions because the

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.459
people running them are attempting

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.289
the impossible: planning

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.809
the future for billions of people.

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.669
Humiliating to preside as it may be,

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.169
Hayek wrote in the Constitution of

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:15.170
Liberty.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.099
The fear of a great escape of losing

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.319
control is understandable

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.729
because there are systemic risks

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.139
that could destroy human

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.149
civilization, including future

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:39.069
natural or manmade pandemics,

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:41.079
runaway inflation and ecological

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:41.979
disaster.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.869
Small boats may not survive a

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.629
storm, but a giant ship

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.519
is strong enough to brave a storm.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.899
But if we're all stuck in the same

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.479
large ship in the same storm,

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.249
we're all going down with it when

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.169
the winds finally get bad enough.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.389
Concentrated power itself presents

00:07:58.390 --> 00:07:59.739
an existential risk.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.179
A bad intervention applied to

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.829
economies of the entire world at

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.629
once can bring down the entire

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.409
system.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:07.479
But the distributed power and humble

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.159
trial and error of markets and

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.169
decentralized governance brings

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.029
progress in fits and starts

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:14.889
with less risk of total ruin.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.049
What Schwab, Xi and central

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.789
planners around the world miss is

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.199
that when securing the rights of the

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.209
individual comes first, the rest

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:23.649
tends to follow.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:25.029
The great escape from the 20th

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.919
century is underway

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.269
and there might be nothing they can

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:29.589
do to stop it.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:31.299
The question is, do they make

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.158
getting there easy or does it

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:34.159
happen the hard way?

